{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://capstone.example/schemas/member-profile.schema.json",
  "title": "Member profile",
  "description": "The portfolio export a member sends themselves: what they ticked and verified, the hashes of output and files, the documents the team filed, per course against the published ontology, and since R132 the twenty-eight KPIs, the six scores by the published method and the minutes between two recorded stamps per course (capstone-member-profile/2). Unsigned: signature is null until validators exist. The copy a candidate link serves (R124) is the same shape, kept small: a row carries its id and level and only the counters that are not zero (an absent counter is zero); a row's dimension, label and references are absent too and the reader restores them from the published ontology by id (a standards row keeps the references its forms cited; a fact row of the troubleshooting, decisions and execution dimensions keeps its label), and a course may leave out the member’s gaps and raw indicators (abilities), which the KPIs already summarise.",
